# ASCII logs and tape text

User-facing strings (`apilog`, `apierror`, `apitoast`, terminal/tape lines, CLI help) must be **ASCII**. Do not paste Unicode punctuation or arrows into those strings.

## Prohibited in user-facing strings

- Unicode arrows / dashes / ellipsis: `→` `←` `↑` `↓` `—` `–` `…`
- Fancy quotes or other non-ASCII symbols meant as UI chrome

Comments in source may use ASCII `--` / `->` / `...`; prefer those over Unicode there too when easy.

## Required instead

| Meaning | Use |
|---------|-----|
| Right arrow | `$26` |
| Left arrow | `$27` (or `$29` where existing menu copy already uses it) |
| Up arrow | `$24` |
| Down arrow | `$25` |
| Ellipsis | `...` |
| Em/en dash | `-` or `--` |

These `$NN` tokens are ZSS text format codes (same as `drop files $26 input/`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
apilog(device, player, `wanix folder mount ok → /${dst}`)
apilog(device, player, `standing up room…`)

// ✅ GOOD
apilog(device, player, `wanix folder mount ok $26 /${dst}`)
apilog(device, player, `standing up room...`)
```

## Scope

Applies to any string that can reach the player tape, toast, CLI help, or scroll UI. Does not ban Unicode inside book content, fixtures, or third-party data the player authored.
